      "capability": "designer.write.schematic.propose_edits",
      "description": "Batch small schematic edits: place library parts, add net labels / power ports / net portals, and wire existing pins. Do NOT pass coordinates — omit positionNm and wire geometry; the layout is auto-arranged from connectivity and wires are auto-routed when this proposal applies. Just choose components and how their pins connect. Non-destructive, so it auto-applies. To wire freshly-placed parts, run this once to place them, then call designer_get_schematic_connectivity and wire by REF.PIN.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "designId": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "action_id": {
            "type": "string",
