    {
      "name": "designer_propose_schematic_wires",
      "version": "1",
      "effect": "write",
      "capability": "designer.write.schematic.propose_wires",
      "description": "Wire schematic pins together, or connect a pin to a named net. Address pins by \"REF.PIN\" (e.g. \"U1.VCC\", \"R1.2\") — call designer_get_schematic_connectivity first to learn references and pin names. Do NOT pass coordinates: routing is automatic and obstacle-aware. After wiring, the whole sheet is auto-arranged — components are MOVED to group what is now connected and wires re-routed cleanly. Non-destructive, so it auto-applies.",
